1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,129
Everybody can build now.

2
00:00:02,629 --> 00:00:05,322
An app. A website.

3
00:00:05,322 --> 00:00:07,148
A whole business idea.

4
00:00:07,398 --> 00:00:09,755
Stuff that used to take a whole team?

5
00:00:09,755 --> 00:00:12,241
One person and a prompt.

6
00:00:12,441 --> 00:00:15,752
And that’s wild, when you really sit with it.

7
00:00:16,402 --> 00:00:19,002
But here’s the part nobody wants to talk about.

8
00:00:19,252 --> 00:00:20,754
If everybody can build…

9
00:00:20,754 --> 00:00:22,812
building ain’t the advantage anymore.

10
00:00:23,212 --> 00:00:25,322
Nobody cares how fast you made it

11
00:00:25,322 --> 00:00:29,660
if it doesn’t solve a problem.

12
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:32,753
So the question isn’t, “what can you create?”

13
00:00:32,853 --> 00:00:35,328
It’s, “what can you make work?”

14
00:00:35,728 --> 00:00:37,688
Something people need.

15
00:00:37,688 --> 00:00:40,150
Something they actually use.

16
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:41,814
Something worth paying for.

17
00:00:42,414 --> 00:00:44,826
AI changed who gets to build.

18
00:00:44,826 --> 00:00:47,350
It didn’t change why people buy.

19
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:49,324
Quiet Bands.

20
00:00:50,239 --> 00:00:51,662
Build what matters.

